      <file>docs/data-model/sprk-playbookconsumer.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r2/spec.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="1">Do the read-only metadata reads and write notes/012-matter-summary-topic.md.</step>
    <step order="2">Write Add-MatterSummaryColumn.ps1 and Seed-MatterSummaryTopicRegistry.ps1 (idempotent, dev URL parameter, -WhatIf support).</step>
    <step order="3">Ask the owner for the go; after it, run both against dev and record the output.</step>
    <step order="4">Trigger one matter-summary run for a test matter as the test user (through the existing Insights/Console path) and confirm the new column holds the envelope; confirm TopicRegistryTtlLookup returns the seeded TTL; record evidence.</step>
    <step order="5">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` (the bracketed ASCII token is mandatory, the emoji alone is not greppable: task-create Step 5, FAILURE-MODES G-16), set the POML &lt;status&gt; to completed, and run pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1</step>
    <step order="6">If any deviations from plan, document in projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r2/notes/ (decisions go to notes/decisions.md)</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the owner has not given the go, STOP after step 2; do not run either script.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the matter-summary Binding is not a work_product disposition, or the persister does not write the new column after the registry row exists, STOP and escalate with the evidence.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>notes/reuse-scan.md row "Matter AI summary" (owner answer: Insights cache, InsightsPlaybookExecutionCache + TopicRegistryTtlLookup); matter-health's sprk_matter.sprk_performancesummary + registry row c46b940e-… is the precedent. CAPABILITY-INDEX: no column-level row (data, not a component).</existing>
    <extension>sprk_performancesummary cannot be reused: it holds matter-health's envelope and the registry maps one topic per target field. The registry, Binding and persister are reused unchanged; only one column and one row are added.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>The matter-summary Binding has nowhere to persist, so spaarke_get_matter_summary (task 032) never finds a cached summary and FR-10's "cached summary in ≤ 3 s" acceptance fails.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="pwsh">scripts/dataverse/*.ps1 (dev, after owner go)</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">scripts/dataverse/Add-MatterSummaryColumn.ps1</output>
    <output type="code">scripts/dataverse/Seed-MatterSummaryTopicRegistry.ps1</output>
    <output type="docs">projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r2/notes/012-matter-summary-topic.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">notes/012-matter-summary-topic.md records the Binding's disposition and capability code, the matter-health registry fields copied, the chosen column name and field-security setting, the owner's go (date) and both script outputs.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Both scripts are idempotent: a second run reports no change.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">After one matter-summary run for a test matter, the new sprk_matter column holds the envelope and TopicRegistryTtlLookup returns the seeded TTL for the topic.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: without the owner's go, no script ran against dev (note states it).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no file under src/server/** changed.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>BLOCKED (code complete, pending owner decision), 2026-11-25: dev already has the Binding (work_product), the registry row (target sprk_recordsummary, TTL 60) and the column, so no column or seed was needed; see notes/012-matter-summary-topic.md. Owner decides whether to run scripts/dataverse/Set-MatterSummaryTopicRegistryKey.ps1 (sprk_playbookname chat-summarize to matter-summary so TopicRegistryTtlLookup finds the TTL). rework: none task 012. Original notes: Spec FR-10 prerequisite, Assumptions ("Insights topic"). The column also needs to ship in the Dataverse solution for other environments: record that as a follow-up for the solution export (dataverse-deploy) in notes, not here.</notes>

